- Yes, of course it does.

209
00:11:23,892 --> 00:11:28,729
Oh, my God, Thom, this right here,
this is exactly the problem.

210
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:32,816
I am the one breaking up with you.
It's me doing this, and I'm sorry, but--

211
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,861
You don't think that this is real
because we're teenagers.

212
00:11:35,862 --> 00:11:37,572
No, no, no.

213
00:11:38,323 --> 00:11:41,367
I don't think that this is real
because it's not.

214
00:11:42,744 --> 00:11:44,579
I'm not in love with you anymore.

215
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:50,042
Hey. [clears throat]

216
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:52,336
Ex-- Can you bring me a steak knife?

217
00:11:52,337 --> 00:11:53,338
Yes, sir.

218
00:12:02,597 --> 00:12:04,139
- No, hey, hey, hey, no, no. Sit down.
- No. No.

219
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,432
- Sit down.
- No. You let go of me.

220
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:06,434
Sit down!

221
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:08,394
Here you go, sir.

222
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:22,659
It's this one right here.

223
00:12:24,327 --> 00:12:26,079
We can go in the bathroom and do it.

224
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:29,623
No one will notice. It won't hurt.

225
00:12:29,624 --> 00:12:32,418
It'll be like drifting off to sleep
in a warm bath.

226
00:12:38,758 --> 00:12:39,926
This one?

227
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,302
Right here?

228
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:44,597
We can hold each other as we go.

229
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:50,228
And once we're gone,
we can meet in the ether as one.

230
00:12:57,652 --> 00:12:58,695
Give me the knife.

231
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:15,544
Fuck you, Thom.

232
00:13:15,545 --> 00:13:16,878
Fuck you.

233
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:18,047
What is wrong with you?

234
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:21,049
You think that I would end my life

235
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:23,385
on some shit-stained
linoleum bathroom floor

236
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:27,597
at the fucking Hamburger Hamlet
for a guy who peaks his senior year?

237
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:30,225
Don't… Don't say…
Don't you ever say that to me.

238
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:33,437
You don't mean that. This is not…
This is Robert in your head.

239
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:37,482
I don't need Robert. I don't need him.
Don't you get it? I don't need anyone.

240
00:13:37,483 --> 00:13:39,651
I have potential.

241
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:42,655
I have a big life to live.

242
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:44,782
I have dreams.

243
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:49,078
We're done, Thom.

244
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:54,751
We're done.

245
00:13:58,379 --> 00:14:00,172
- I'm leaving.
- No. We're not…

246
00:14:00,173 --> 00:14:02,674
- We're not done talking.
- Yeah, I'm leaving. I'm leaving.

247
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:04,718
- You're sick.
- I know.

248
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:07,512
I can change. I'll be different.
I'll be whoever you want me to be.

249
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:10,933
Just tell me how you want me to be.
I can be that. I'll be different. Tell me.

250
00:14:12,727 --> 00:14:16,897
I… I don't want you to be different.

251
00:14:16,898 --> 00:14:18,983
I want you to be you.

252
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:24,530
- I hate myself.
- No, you are perfect, okay?

253
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:28,326
Then why doesn't anyone stay?

254
00:14:29,077 --> 00:14:31,536
You know, if I'm so perfect,
why does everyone abandon me?

255
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:33,956
I'm not abandoning you, Thom.

256
00:14:34,916 --> 00:14:37,667
I'm gonna be in your life
for a very long time.

257
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:38,669
No.

258
00:14:39,921 --> 00:14:41,172
You won't be.

259
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:43,591
The lovers die.

260
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:48,763
Are you threatening me?

261
00:14:51,057 --> 00:14:53,309
I'm just reminding you how the story ends.

262
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,493
[sniffles]

263
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,584
[sniffles]

264
00:15:37,979 --> 00:15:41,231
<i>Macbeth</i>, Act 4, Scene 3.

265
00:15:41,232 --> 00:15:43,191
"Let's make us medicines
of our great revenge

266
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:44,902
to cure this deadly grief."

267
00:15:45,862 --> 00:15:46,863
Makes sense to me.

268
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:50,532
As long as you're feeling potent,

269
00:15:50,533 --> 00:15:53,410
you're feeling something other than sad.

270
00:15:53,411 --> 00:15:55,705
Revenge as a cure for depression.

271
00:15:57,039 --> 00:16:00,167
But if revenge is a medicine,
there are definitely some side effects.

272
00:16:00,168 --> 00:16:02,086
Who can tell me
the potential side effects?

273
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:03,796
Chaos.

274
00:16:04,422 --> 00:16:06,257
[Ms. Rogers] Chaos, sure.

275
00:16:07,425 --> 00:16:09,468
Seriously though, think about it.

276
00:16:10,303 --> 00:16:13,430
What would happen if you hurt
the people who hurt you?

277
00:16:13,431 --> 00:16:14,432
[Robert] They'd hurt him back.

278
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:17,226
"Blood will have blood."

279
00:16:19,729 --> 00:16:20,730
Act 3, scene 4.

280
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:25,192
[Ms. Rogers] Bingo. Revenge unleashes
an endless cycle of counterstrikes

281
00:16:25,193 --> 00:16:29,112
and counter-counterstrikes,
as <i>Macbeth</i> more than proves.

282
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:33,074
Blood will have blood
until everyone's bled out.

283
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:35,285
So it's like a tie?

284
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:38,456
No. Everyone loses in the end.

285
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:43,085
Everyone loses.

286
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,758
[♪ dramatic synth music plays]

287
00:16:49,759 --> 00:16:53,137
[Ms. Rogers] <i>Lady Macbeth is
one of the great villains of literature.</i>

288
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:58,643
<i>But does she even understand
the domino effects of her plotting?</i>

289
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:04,940
<i>"By the pricking of thumbs,
something wicked this way comes."</i>

290
00:17:04,941 --> 00:17:06,524
- [gasps]
- Mmm.

291
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:10,487
You are so gorgeous. Oh, my God.

292
00:17:10,488 --> 00:17:11,947
[♪ pop music plays on speakers]

293
00:17:11,948 --> 00:17:13,032
- Hi.
- Mmm.

294
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:17,327
- Thank God my pharmacist is here.
- [chuckles]

295
00:17:17,328 --> 00:17:19,246
Mama is running low.

296
00:17:19,247 --> 00:17:22,207
I've just been a nervous wreck
with this whole Trawler thing.

297
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:23,291
[Steven] Oh.

298
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:26,336
Terry says we're installing
some new security system,

299
00:17:26,337 --> 00:17:28,798
and I have to come up with
a four-digit password.

300
00:17:29,507 --> 00:17:31,968
But how the hell
am I ever going to remember that?

301
00:17:33,970 --> 00:17:36,680
I'm losing sleep just knowing

302
00:17:36,681 --> 00:17:39,975
that there's this horrible monster
out there targeting kids.

303
00:17:39,976 --> 00:17:41,435
Well, you know,

304
00:17:42,478 --> 00:17:45,064
every monster has their reason
they became one.

305
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:48,776
So, down to business.

306
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:54,948
I've gone ahead and replenished
your supply of Valium

307
00:17:54,949 --> 00:17:59,202
- and Halcion. [chuckles]
- [chuckles]

308
00:17:59,203 --> 00:18:03,040
I don't like the pill bottles
pharmacies use. Plastic and ugly.

309
00:18:03,833 --> 00:18:06,210
You are a woman of value.

310
00:18:07,003 --> 00:18:09,380
- You really do think of everything.
- [chuckles]

311
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:13,342
I have news.

312
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:17,596
I have been watching
the staff at the house lately,

313
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:19,222
and in my opinion,

314
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:23,394
you are not being treated
with the respect that you deserve.

315
00:18:24,854 --> 00:18:30,860
So, I took it upon myself
to distribute a memo to the help.

316
00:18:34,739 --> 00:18:38,325
From now on,
you will be addressed as Ms. Schaffer,

317
00:18:38,326 --> 00:18:40,702
not Mrs. Schaffer.

318
00:18:40,703 --> 00:18:44,540
People should see
that Terry does not define you.

319
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,960
This town runs
on the backs of women like you.

320
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:50,378
[scoffs]

321
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:51,963
It's true.

322
00:18:51,964 --> 00:18:54,342
I crawled through glass, Steven,

323
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:56,718
with a smile on my face

324
00:18:56,719 --> 00:18:59,930
and a Miss Indiana sash
choking me out along the way.

325
00:19:00,431 --> 00:19:03,225
I find it calming
to be placed on a pedestal.

326
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:05,644
Even if it's yours.

327
00:19:05,645 --> 00:19:06,937
So thank you for that.

328
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:10,941
Well,

329
00:19:12,777 --> 00:19:16,405
say goodbye
to that momentary peace, Ms. Schaffer,

330
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:21,702
because I'm about to say something
that may destabilize you.

331
00:19:23,788 --> 00:19:24,789
Don't scream.

332
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:27,083
Don't make a scene.

333
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:29,668
Just listen.

334
00:19:29,669 --> 00:19:30,961
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

335
00:19:34,131 --> 00:19:36,300
I know about the porno film.

336
00:19:39,095 --> 00:19:40,345
What porno?

337
00:19:40,346 --> 00:19:46,310
Oh, honey, I've seen you do things
the human body has no business attempting.

338
00:19:47,687 --> 00:19:48,854
How did you see it?

339
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:53,108
They promised me
it would only be an overseas release.

340
00:19:53,109 --> 00:19:55,777
If Echo Park Lake can be considered a sea,

341
00:19:55,778 --> 00:19:57,529
then they have indeed.

342
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:58,531
What?

343
00:20:00,950 --> 00:20:02,367
It's playing in town here?

344
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:05,704
You and little baby Ryan
on a silver screen

345
00:20:05,705 --> 00:20:08,416
that grows more tarnished
with each showing.

346
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:11,961
[gasps] Oh, my God, what have I done?

347
00:20:12,712 --> 00:20:13,795
Terry will leave me.

348
00:20:13,796 --> 00:20:16,923
I'll have no money.
Oh, my God, I'll have no money.

349
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:19,176
Take a Halcion, honey. It'll help.

350
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:21,178
[Liz exhales sharply]

351
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:26,726
If you even think
about telling anyone about this,

352
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:29,729
so help me God,

353
00:20:31,439 --> 00:20:33,606
you don't know what I'm capable of.

354
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:34,816
Stop.

355
00:20:34,817 --> 00:20:36,569
Just stop it right now.

356
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:41,824
Of course your secret is safe with me.

357
00:20:45,119 --> 00:20:47,788
I just want to know why you did it.

358
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:51,250
- [♪ pop music plays on speakers]
- [chattering]

359
00:20:54,879 --> 00:20:56,213
[Liz] I don't know.

360
00:20:58,591 --> 00:21:00,509
I don't even know who I am anymore.

361
00:21:02,887 --> 00:21:04,597
Or why I do what I do.

362
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:09,101
I'm just an object now.

363
00:21:13,189 --> 00:21:17,692
It was the vengeful impulse
of a rusty trophy, the dirty movie.

364
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:20,154
- That's all.
- Are you sure about that?

365
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:24,282
Maybe I wanted to be touched again

366
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:26,534
even if it was only in a scene
we were playing.

367
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:29,829
Spare me <i>The Day of The Locust</i> act, Liz.
I ain't buying it.

368
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:32,583
Uh, one final round, please. Thank you.

369
00:21:34,627 --> 00:21:39,548
I think there's something bubbling beneath
the constantly turbulent surface here.

370
00:21:40,174 --> 00:21:41,758
I can see your daydreams.

371
00:21:41,759 --> 00:21:43,676
I know you want to act,

372
00:21:43,677 --> 00:21:46,262
and I think this was
just a perverse attempt

373
00:21:46,263 --> 00:21:48,264
at moving towards that dream.

374
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:49,683
[♪ dramatic music plays]

375
00:21:51,936 --> 00:21:54,063
"Out, damned spot. Out, I say.

376
00:21:55,773 --> 00:21:57,775
One, two.

377
00:21:58,818 --> 00:22:01,445
Why, then 'tis time to do it.

378
00:22:02,655 --> 00:22:04,365
Hell is murky."

379
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:07,034
[chuckles]

380
00:22:08,953 --> 00:22:13,082
"False face must hide
what the false heart doth know."

381
00:22:18,337 --> 00:22:21,840
I want you to know
that I purchased every negative,

382
00:22:21,841 --> 00:22:25,426
so you don't have to worry
about it ever seeing the light of day.

383
00:22:25,427 --> 00:22:28,596
And to protect you from your husband.

384
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:30,015
Oh, Steven.

385
00:22:31,141 --> 00:22:32,768
Oh, my God, thank you.

386
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:36,814
But I'm gonna hold on to them, though, sweetie.

387
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:41,986
[sighs]
'Cause I got to look out for myself.

388
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:47,700
- What do you want?
- What I deserve.

389
00:22:48,492 --> 00:22:51,160
Terry doesn't see me
as a contender in this industry,

390
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:55,791
so I'm gonna need your help
in bringing to life a grand vision.

391
00:22:56,375 --> 00:23:01,005
A film called <i>Less Than Zero,</i>
and I'm going to produce with him.

392
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:05,717
Debbie's boyfriend Bret wrote a treatment
based on a novel he's writing.

393
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:07,302
It's brilliant.

394
00:23:07,303 --> 00:23:10,346
I wrote glowing coverage,
and Terry wouldn't even read it.

395
00:23:10,347 --> 00:23:12,515
Liz, he doesn't fucking read.

396
00:23:12,516 --> 00:23:14,934
He just took
a bullshit meeting with Mr. Ellis,

397
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:16,270
but he's not gonna close the rights.

398
00:23:17,438 --> 00:23:19,023
You are gonna help me get them.

399
00:23:19,899 --> 00:23:24,277
There's a role for you in the project.
You are perfect for it.

400
00:23:24,278 --> 00:23:28,240
Become, at long last, a star.

401
00:23:30,701 --> 00:23:33,578
- What do you need me to do?
- Every night while Terry sleeps,

402
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:35,788
I need you to whisper
a single sentence into his ear

403
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:37,666
no fewer than 100 times,

404
00:23:38,459 --> 00:23:42,087
just like Nancy does with Ronnie Reagan
to get her little plans in his head.

405
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:44,672
What is the sentence?

406
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:50,387
<i>"Less Than Zero</i>
will make you $100 million."

407
00:24:06,111 --> 00:24:08,321
[Bret] <i>Our next lesson was on</i> Hamlet,

408
00:24:08,322 --> 00:24:11,532
<i>and the parallels
to my increasingly unrecognizable life</i>

409
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:14,870
<i>were so blinding
that I couldn't help but feel mocked.</i>

410
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:18,414
<i>We were both princes.</i>

411
00:24:18,415 --> 00:24:20,166
<i>We were both secretive,</i>

412
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:22,502
<i>and we both knew
that something very rotten</i>

413
00:24:22,503 --> 00:24:25,213
<i>- was afoot within our own kingdoms.</i>
- [school bell rings]

414
00:24:25,214 --> 00:24:28,883
[Ms. Rogers] All right, I need
Acts 1 through 3 read before next class.

415
00:24:28,884 --> 00:24:30,344
[students chattering]

416
00:24:31,387 --> 00:24:33,972
And I want 500 words
on how Shakespeare is commenting

417
00:24:33,973 --> 00:24:36,725
on the connection between
mortality and madness.

418
00:24:37,768 --> 00:24:38,894
Thank you.

419
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:46,694
Bret, you have a second?

420
00:24:47,277 --> 00:24:50,446
- We should talk. In private.
- [Fregosi] Would it be all right

421
00:24:50,447 --> 00:24:53,242
if we asked you for this classroom
for just a few minutes?

422
00:24:54,535 --> 00:24:56,661
All right. Though I do have
another class in here shortly.

423
00:24:56,662 --> 00:24:57,663
Shouldn't be long.

424
00:24:58,247 --> 00:24:59,540
[Ms. Rogers] Sure.

425
00:25:01,542 --> 00:25:02,876
[door closes]

426
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:06,005
We got some more questions for you
about Matt Kellner.

427
00:25:07,673 --> 00:25:09,007
What kind of questions?

428
00:25:09,008 --> 00:25:11,427
Questions about
your personal relationship with Matt.

429
00:25:13,053 --> 00:25:15,139
[Bret] My personal relationship with Matt?

430
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:18,934
We were just acquaintances.

431
00:25:19,518 --> 00:25:20,853
Not even close, really.

432
00:25:21,478 --> 00:25:24,022
If you want to speak with someone
who was close with Matt,

433
00:25:24,023 --> 00:25:25,773
I suggest talking to Robert Mallory
about him.

434
00:25:25,774 --> 00:25:28,902
We already have talked
to Robert Mallory about him, extensively.

435
00:25:29,987 --> 00:25:33,114
Let me ask you a question, Bret.
Did you go to the Kellner house

436
00:25:33,115 --> 00:25:34,616
on the day that Matt disappeared?

437
00:25:35,784 --> 00:25:37,369
You didn't tell us that before.

438
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:40,080
I didn't think it was significant.

439
00:25:40,706 --> 00:25:44,042
We were discussing a class assignment.
He needed help with it.

440
00:25:44,043 --> 00:25:46,085
[Fregosi] There was another thing
you didn't tell us.

441
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:49,130
You visited Matt's father
after his disappearance.

442
00:25:49,131 --> 00:25:50,631
[♪ ominous music plays]

443
00:25:50,632 --> 00:25:52,926
I-I just didn't think it was relevant.

444
00:25:54,678 --> 00:25:55,845
Why did you?

445
00:25:55,846 --> 00:25:59,265
- Out of concern for my friend.
- [Fregosi] I thought you weren't friends.

446
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:01,893
Which is it?
Were you or were you not friends?

447
00:26:01,894 --> 00:26:02,895
Or…

448
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:08,317
were you something else altogether?

449
00:26:08,901 --> 00:26:11,152
[Donaldson]
Inconsistencies are not always meaningful,

450
00:26:11,153 --> 00:26:15,032
but when they're attributed to the person
who found the victim's body…

451
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:21,205
yeah, then we feel obligated
to maybe dig a little deeper.

452
00:26:23,582 --> 00:26:24,917
Of course.

453
00:26:26,460 --> 00:26:28,503
Is that all, officers?

454
00:26:28,504 --> 00:26:31,590
Hmm. There is one more.

455
00:26:32,132 --> 00:26:34,509
You were overheard
on the soundstage of <i>Dance Off!</i>

456
00:26:34,510 --> 00:26:38,054
whispering to Debbie Schaffer
that she deserved to win.

457
00:26:38,055 --> 00:26:40,766
How badly
did you want your girlfriend to win, Bret?

458
00:26:42,184 --> 00:26:44,478
Are you implying that I killed Cha Cha?

459
00:26:45,395 --> 00:26:46,896
[school bell rings]

460
00:26:46,897 --> 00:26:49,065
Where is this coming from?
Am I under arrest?

461
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:51,109
- Should you be?
- [door opens]

462
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:54,071
[Ms. Rogers]
Officers, I need my classroom back now.

463
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:58,158
No worries, ma'am.
We were just finishing up here.

464
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:02,996
Thank you, ma'am.

465
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:09,085
[Bret] <i>My secrets were catching up to me.</i>

466
00:27:09,086 --> 00:27:11,712
<i>My anxiety from concealing my sexuality</i>

467
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:13,966
<i>had inadvertently led
to becoming a suspect.</i>

468
00:27:15,384 --> 00:27:16,635
<i>I didn't have an alibi.</i>

469
00:27:17,219 --> 00:27:18,220
<i>I was fucked.</i>

470
00:27:18,887 --> 00:27:21,389
<i>Someone was coloring
their perception of me,</i>

471
00:27:21,390 --> 00:27:23,267
<i>and I knew exactly who that was.</i>

472
00:27:26,478 --> 00:27:27,688
[crickets chirping]

473
00:27:34,778 --> 00:27:35,779
[keys jangling]

474
00:27:56,592 --> 00:27:57,717
[thudding]

475
00:27:57,718 --> 00:27:59,928
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

476
00:28:07,603 --> 00:28:09,187
[clicking switches]

477
00:29:01,531 --> 00:29:02,991
[Bret breathes shakily]

478
00:29:07,704 --> 00:29:09,747
[banging on window]

479
00:29:09,748 --> 00:29:12,250
Robert, I know it's you.

480
00:29:31,436 --> 00:29:34,231
- [electricity surges]
- [vehicle engine starts in distance]

481
00:29:37,985 --> 00:29:39,361
[engine fades]

482
00:30:17,065 --> 00:30:18,983
[Bret] <i>I thought that nothing
could terrify me more</i>

483
00:30:18,984 --> 00:30:21,027
<i>than being framed
for Matt Kellner's murder.</i>

484
00:30:21,028 --> 00:30:22,154
- [static]
- [beeping]

485
